UPDATE scholarships SET title = $$IIT Delhi - 'International Excellence Scholarship' is an importer-invented name; no verified award (retired)$$, provider = $$Indian Institute of Technology Delhi (IIT Delhi)$$, country = $$India$$, coverage_type = $$Unspecified$$, amount_usd_value = 0, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, deadline = $$Retired - no award of this (importer-invented) name exists on IIT Delhi's official pages and no application round applies. Foreign nationals apply to IITD programmes through the institute's international admissions channels (see description).$$ , deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = $$not_published$$, opening_date = NULL, deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, rounds = $$[]$$, recurrence = $$none$$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, degree_levels = $$["Master's", "PhD"]$$, eligible_majors = $$["All Majors"]$$, eligible_countries = $$["RETIRED - no verified scheme; the 'GPA 3.7+ / IELTS 6.5+' profile previously stored here was importer text with no official source"]$$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $$RETIRED in Pass 119 (2026-10-28). "IIT Delhi International Excellence Scholarship" is an importer-invented name (the recurring fabricated "International Excellence Scholarship" suffix): no award of this name appears on IIT Delhi's fetched official pages, and the previously stored profile (GPA 3.7+, IELTS 6.5+) had no official source. What the fetched official pages DO establish: (1) foreign nationals apply to IITD PhD/PG programmes through the institute's international admissions portal (IPGADM) in semester cycles - PhD admissions are normally advertised in March and October - and the International Programmes office states that offline PhD applications for international candidates are accepted throughout the year; (2) registration on the Government of India's Study in India portal is mandatory for all foreign students before applying for a student visa; (3) IITD operates a Teaching/Research Assistantship scheme under which non-sponsored full-time PhD students are considered for assistantships at INR 37,000 per month for the first two years and INR 42,000 per month for the next three (fetched from the official DMS PhD admissions page, new source 3124). What could NOT be verified first-hand in this pass: IITD's foreign-student-specific "Fees & Financial Support" page (international.iitd.ac.in/78-2/) - whose search-visible text claims that all full-time foreign PhD admits are awarded the assistantship and that foreign MTech/MDes/MS(R) students may receive limited merit assistantships of INR 12,400/month, consistent with the IPFP fee/fellowship-parity policy reported at its 2019 launch - failed to fetch in four attempts (as did the archived launch page and the intladm portal, HTTP 403). Snippet-only claims are never encoded in this catalogue, so the record is retired until that official page (or the PG information brochure) can be read first-hand; revive then as a properly named IITD foreign-student funding record.$$ , requirements = $$Do not apply on the basis of this record - it is retired and the named award does not exist. Foreign nationals interested in IIT Delhi should: register on the Study in India portal (mandatory before the student visa, per the International Programmes office); apply for PhD/PG admission through the foreign-national application channel in the semester cycles (PhD normally advertised in March and October; offline international PhD applications are also accepted throughout the year per the office); and read the current foreign-student funding rules on IITD's Fees & Financial Support page and the PG information brochure before assuming any assistantship - the institute's general Teaching/Research Assistantship for non-sponsored full-time PhD students pays INR 37,000/month (first two years) and INR 42,000/month (next three) per the fetched DMS page, but the foreign-national entitlement itself was not verifiable first-hand in this pass. The ICCR route via Indian embassies is the standard alternative support channel for foreign students in India.$$ , website_url = $$https://international.iitd.ac.in/$$, source_url = $$https://international.iitd.ac.in/$$, application_url = $$https://international.iitd.ac.in/$$, funding_type = $$RETIRED - importer-invented scholarship name; IITD's foreign-student funding terms could not be verified first-hand (official Fees & Financial Support page unreachable in this pass)$$, tuition_coverage = $$RETIRED - no coverage can be stated: the named award does not exist and the foreign-specific fee/assistantship rules were not read first-hand.$$ , living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, application_fee = NULL, english_requirements = $$Not applicable - retired record; the previously stored IELTS 6.5 was importer text.$$ , required_documents = $$[]$$, application_status = $$closed$$, verification_status = $$verified$$, source_reliability = 9, is_active = false, university_id = 108, notes = $$PASS 119 RETIREMENT 2026-10-28 (India cluster): 'International Excellence Scholarship' is the recurring importer-invented suffix (cf. rows 467/466/503/502); IITD publishes no award of this name on the fetched official pages (International Programmes homepage chunks 0-1; DMS PhD admissions page chunks 0-1, new source 3124). Stored min_gpa 3.7 / min_ielts 6.5 (echoed in us 496) were sourceless importer text - removed. FETCH LOG for the defining foreign-student funding page: international.iitd.ac.in/78-2/ failed 4x (plain, /index.php/78-2/, no-trailing-slash), old.iitd.ac.in IPFP launch page failed, intladm.iitd.ac.in returned 403. Search-visible official-domain text for 78-2 claims TAs for all full-time foreign PhD admits (INR 37,000 -> 42,000) and limited INR 12,400 master's TAs, matching the 2019 IPFP parity launch reports - deliberately NOT encoded from snippets (same standard as the IUM enweb and POSCO decisions). REVIVAL PATH: when 78-2 or the PG information brochure fetches cleanly, create/re-anchor a properly named IITD foreign-national assistantship record from that text. Fetched anchors banked: foreign PhD cycles (advertised Mar/Oct; Sem-II 2026-27 foreign deadline 29.10.2026 per DMS), year-round offline international PhD applications (International Programmes office), Study-in-India registration mandate, TA rates for non-sponsored full-time PhD (INR 37,000/42,000). us 496 deleted; root source link 826 retained for audit; (477, 3124) added.$$ , last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 477;

